      "title": "make_transaction creates the standard record",
      "description": "Create make_transaction(transaction_id, amount_paise, category, description, date_text, kind) in expense_manager/make.py. A transaction has the shape {\"id\": 1, \"amount_paise\": 1250, \"category\": \"food\", \"description\": \"tea\", \"date\": \"2026-10-10\", \"kind\": \"expense\"}. Use validate_transaction_values from expense_manager/transaction_validation.py and normalize_transaction_text from expense_manager/transaction_text.py (already written, shown below).\n1. if not isinstance(transaction_id, int) or isinstance(transaction_id, bool) or transaction_id <= 0: raise ValueError\n2. values_ok = validate_transaction_values(amount_paise, date_text, kind)\n3. text_fields = normalize_transaction_text(category, description)\n4. return {\"id\": transaction_id, \"amount_paise\": amount_paise, \"category\": text_fields[\"category\"], \"description\": text_fields[\"description\"], \"date\": date_text, \"kind\": kind}\n",
      "commit": "feat: construct transaction records",
