      "description": "Create replace_transaction(transactions, transaction_id, updated_transaction) in expense_manager/replace.py. Transactions and updated_transaction use the standard transaction shape {\"id\": 1, \"amount_paise\": 1250, \"category\": \"food\", \"description\": \"tea\", \"date\": \"2026-10-10\", \"kind\": \"expense\"}. Use find_transaction from expense_manager/find.py (already written, shown below). Return a NEW list and copy every record dictionary.\n1. found = find_transaction(transactions, transaction_id)\n2. if updated_transaction[\"id\"] != transaction_id: raise ValueError\n3. result = []\n4. For each item in transactions:\n   - if item[\"id\"] == transaction_id: result.append(dict(updated_transaction))\n   - else: result.append(dict(item))\n5. return result\n",
